.\" man page create by R# package system.
.TH GSVA 1 2000-1月 "multiple_dataset" "multiple_dataset"
.SH NAME
multiple_dataset \- Assemble the multiple omics data layers into a [MultiOmicsDataset](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.HTS.GSVA.Omics.MultiOmicsDataset) object
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fImultiple_dataset(\fBlayers\fR as any, 
\fBverbose\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Assemble the multiple omics data layers into a [MultiOmicsDataset](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.HTS.GSVA.Omics.MultiOmicsDataset) object
 for the multi-omics GSVA (moGSVA) analysis.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBlayers\fB \fR\- 
 the omics layer collection, each element could be an [OmicsLayer](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.HTS.DataFrame.MultipleOmics.OmicsLayer) object or
 a tuple that could be cast into the omics layer model. Every layer should define its
 unique omics name and the expression matrix whose rows are the features of that omics.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBverbose\fB \fR\- prints the progress and the diagnostic message of the layer alignment? Default \fBTRUE\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a [MultiOmicsDataset](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.HTS.GSVA.Omics.MultiOmicsDataset) object which contains the sample aligned omics layers,
 or an error message when the layer collection could not be assembled.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
The samples of all of the omics layers are aligned by the sample name: the intersection
 of the sample names is used as the final sample axis of the multi-omics dataset.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
GSVA
.SH FILES
.PP
gseakit.dll
.PP
